cal/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wBnk6P/translation/src/blake512.rs`**\n- Renamed the private `const C512: [u64; 16]` to `#[no_mangle] pub static cst: [u64; 16]` (single source of truth — all 12 internal call sites now read `cst`). Values were already identical to `c_src/lib/blake/src/blake512.c:45`.\n\nNothing under `c_src/` was touched.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll 48 feature combos: `cargo check` passes, zero warnings.\n\n```\n0000000000019ce0 T AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update\n000000000001a160 T AES256_ECB\n0000000000059ca4 B DRBG_ctx\n000000000000a290 R cst\n000000000001c660 T seedexpander\n000000000001c880 T seedexpander_init\n```\n\nDriver digest unchanged: `97B452A98F312321D982CDE133B1BF6D7189DC0A9296338C9A823A6689670584`\n\n## Extra checks I ran (temporary harness, since deleted)\n\n- **Symbol metadata matches C exactly**: `DRBG_ctx` size `0x34` (52) type `B`; `cst` size `0x80` (128) type `R` — identical to `libsphincs_core_det.so` / `libblake.so`.\n- **`cst` contents**: extracted the 128 raw bytes from both `.so` files' `.rodata` — identical.\n- **Differential test**: a `dlopen`-based harness exercising all six symbols against both the C `libsphincs_core_det.so` and the Rust `.so` produced **identical** output, covering `AES256_ECB`, `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` (with and without `provided_data`), `seedexpander_init` (including `-1` on oversized `maxlen`), `seedexpander` (`-2` for NULL, `-3` for oversized request, plus buffer-straddling reads), `randombytes(NULL, 0)`, and `DRBG_ctx` state read through the exported global. Notably the test dumped the whole 80-byte `AES_XOF_struct` as raw bytes before and after use, so field layout, padding, buffer zeroing, and `buffer_pos`/`length_remaining` all match bit-for-bit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2418,"cache_read_input_tokens":68834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2418,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_token