{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a172d91530f5b6444","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QWsVk3CptKuw8zpWsV6YrL","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-4iyHMm/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-wBnk6P/ad09d3fe-ada9-47ca-9d56-2e4ee9154101/tasks/a172d91530f5b6444.output","summary":"Done. All 6 missing symbols are now exported, verified byte-for-byte against the C `.so`s.\n\n## Files changed\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wBnk6P/translation/src/rng.rs`**\n- Removed `use std::sync::Mutex;` and the private `struct Drbg` + `static DRBG: Mutex<Drbg>`.\n- Added `#[repr(C)] pub struct AES256_CTR_DRBG_struct { Key: [u8;32], V: [u8;16], reseed_counter: c_int }` with `const _` asserts for size 52 / align 4, and `#[no_mangle] pub static mut DRBG_ctx` as the **real** state (zero-initialised, lands in `.bss`).\n- `randombytes_init` / `randombytes` now operate on `DRBG_ctx` directly via `addr_of_mut!` (no `static_mut_refs` errors, no warnings). `randombytes` delegates to a new `unsafe fn randombytes_raw(*mut u8, u64)` that uses `copy_nonoverlapping` instead of building a slice, so `randombytes(NULL, 0)` is well-defined and still performs the DRBG update + `reseed_counter` increment.\n- `AesXofStruct` is now `#[repr(C)]` with `buffer_pos: u64`; added `const _` asserts for size 80, align 8, and offsets 0/16/24/32/64.\n- `seedexpander` logic moved into `unsafe fn seedexpander_raw(*mut AesXofStruct, *mut u8, u64)` with the NULL check **before** the length check (`-2` then `-3`); the safe `seedexpander(&mut _, &mut [u8])` wraps it.\n- `seedexpander_init` keeps the `memset(ctx->buffer, 0, 16)` — I confirmed in the C source (`rng.c` line ~48) that C *does* zero the buffer and *does* set `buffer_pos = 16`, so the existing Rust was already correct there.\n- New exports: `AES256_ECB`, `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` (raw-pointer body transcribed literally from C, NULL `provided_data` handled), `seedexpander_init` (with the `maxlen >= 0x100000000` check hoisted into the wrapper so it returns `-1` before touching any pointer, as C does), `seedexpander`.\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wBnk6P/translation/src/blake512.rs`**\n- Renamed the private `const C512: [u64; 16]` to `#[no_mangle] pub static cst: [u64; 16]` (single source of truth — all 12 internal call sites now read `cst`). Values were already identical to `c_src/lib/blake/src/blake512.c:45`.\n\nNothing under `c_src/` was touched.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll 48 feature combos: `cargo check` passes, zero warnings.\n\n```\n0000000000019ce0 T AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update\n000000000001a160 T AES256_ECB\n0000000000059ca4 B DRBG_ctx\n000000000000a290 R cst\n000000000001c660 T seedexpander\n000000000001c880 T seedexpander_init\n```\n\nDriver digest unchanged: `97B452A98F312321D982CDE133B1BF6D7189DC0A9296338C9A823A6689670584`\n\n## Extra checks I ran (temporary harness, since deleted)\n\n- **Symbol metadata matches C exactly**: `DRBG_ctx` size `0x34` (52) type `B`; `cst` size `0x80` (128) type `R` — identical to `libsphincs_core_det.so` / `libblake.so`.\n- **`cst` contents**: extracted the 128 raw bytes from both `.so` files' `.rodata` — identical.\n- **Differential test**: a `dlopen`-based harness exercising all six symbols against both the C `libsphincs_core_det.so` and the Rust `.so` produced **identical** output, covering `AES256_ECB`, `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` (with and without `provided_data`), `seedexpander_init` (including `-1` on oversized `maxlen`), `seedexpander` (`-2` for NULL, `-3` for oversized request, plus buffer-straddling reads), `randombytes(NULL, 0)`, and `DRBG_ctx` state read through the exported global. Notably the test dumped the whole 80-byte `AES_XOF_struct` as raw bytes before and after use, so field layout, padding, buffer zeroing, and `buffer_pos`/`length_remaining` all match bit-for-bit.","usage":{"total_tokens":72426,"tool_uses":32,"duration_ms":342378},"